Recap from the Pinewood call (1:00-1:55). Moving them Discovery -> Scoping in the sheet.

Who: Lucia Ferraro (VP Ops), Dale Ruiz (Turlock plant manager), two schedulers from Turlock. Four plants total (Turlock, Modesto, Merced, Los Banos).

Pain: schedulers rebuild the shift board by hand from the ERP export every morning; late lots on the packaging lines get found at end of shift, not during. Dale's line: "we find out we were late when the truck's already gone."

What they want: a six-week pilot at Turlock, scoped by end of March; exception alerts + shift board; two customer references before they sign anything. Lucia asked twice about implementation time; Hana said 3-4 weeks to first data on a plant with a nightly ERP export, which they already have (quick win).

Next:
- Hana + me: scoping doc draft by Mar 13, walk-through with Lucia's team the week after.
- NDA: they'll want ours before we see plant data.
- References: parked until you say so.

No pricing talk, as agreed. Lucia tried once. I changed the subject to cheese.

